## The Tale of Fizzwick & Felicia

Fizzwick Geargrind, a gnome warlock barely taller than a worg, puffed out his chest as Felicia, his succubus, effortlessly dispatched another panthara. Stranglethorn Vale was… humid. And full of things that wanted to eat him. "Honestly, Felicia, you make this look *too* easy," he grumbled, adjusting his oversized goggles. 

Felicia merely smirked, her voice a silken whisper, "Efficiency, little one. Besides, someone has to keep you from accidentally summoning a demon *inside* a tree." 

Their current quest involved collecting spider eggs. Fizzwick was meticulously scanning the webs, while Felicia… was charming the local pirates into handing them over. "A little persuasion goes a long way, darling," she purred, a glint in her eye. Fizzwick sighed. He knew she was far superior for leveling, but the other warlocks insisted Voidwalkers were 'the meta'. He just hoped they wouldn't discover Felicia's… talents.



---

**Answer:** Seduction. Succubi frequently seduce other players, causing them to accidentally dismiss their current pets and summon a Voidwalker instead, leading to their prevalence. [end of text]


